  "evidence_level": {
    "justification": "The admitted object is a derivation about the corrected four-cell discharge equation set (28 rows, 25 unknowns, spec/plasma/equation-ledger.json): substituting the mutually consistent rows R00-R26 into the global power row R27 leaves the closed form 2 (j_e3 (1-p4) + I4)(phi_4 - Ua) + EI (p1 j_e0 + p2 j_e1 + p3 j_e2), whose two terms are non-negative on the admissible region, so no admissible root exists for any positive interior cusp probability. It is neither a preregistered numerical campaign (nothing was executed under a protocol; the numbers are verification of an algebraic identity) nor a design-space screening (no design was screened) nor a physics level (no field, plasma or experimental evidence). The analytic-consistency kind therefore admits it: the closed form is verified numerically to a stated tolerance, pinned by committed tests, and recomputed by the paper checker from the bound package at every run. Status accepted means the derivation and its numerical verification are admitted as recorded; it accepts no correction of the equation set (the proposal stays PROPOSED_NOT_ACCEPTED), makes no statement about the physical thruster, and opens none of GATE-L1, GATE-L2 or GATE-L3.",
    "name": "analytic-consistency",
    "opens_gate": null,
    "relation_to_levels": {
      "L0": "independent of the accepted L0 conservation model; the four-cell ledger is a separate equation set that L0 does not consume",
      "L1": "no field solve, geometry or L0 mapping",
      "L2": "the analysis concerns the candidate coupled plasma equation set; it supplies no coupled model and leaves GATE-L2 closed",
      "L3": "not particle-in-cell and not experimental"
    },
    "validation_status": "none: the result is a property of an equation set, not a comparison with any measurement",
    "verification_tier": "numerical verification of an algebraic identity (closed form versus full residual over a seeded sample; continuation, anode-only closures, published-state misfit, relaxed root, Jacobian rank) recomputed at every check against declared tolerances"
  },
